  "text": "I'm so sorry to hear that you're feeling angry and sad. It's completely normal to feel that way when we feel like our parents are trying to control us.\n\nWhen I was in a similar situation, I remember feeling really frustrated and angry too. But what helped me was talking to my mom about how I felt. I told her that I understood she was coming from a place of love and concern, but that I also needed some space to make my own choices.\n\nIt's not always easy, but sometimes talking about our feelings and needs can help our parents understand where we're coming from. It might not change their opinion right away, but it can help them see things from our perspective.\n\nAlso, it might be helpful to remind yourself that you do have the freedom to choose your friends, even if your mom doesn't approve. You can still be friends with the people you want to be friends with, and it's okay to set boundaries with your mom if you need to.\n\nLastly, remember that you're not alone in this. Many people have had to deal with similar situations, and it's not a reflection of your worth or the quality of your relationships. You are loved and deserving of respect, no matter what.\n\nHow does that sound? Does that help a little bit?",
